// A path that holds a NUL byte is a runtime error for exists
// (spec/05-stdlib.md, Paths): the host reads a path only up to its first NUL
// byte, so the call would answer for a shorter path than the program named.
// A consumer that passes the String through prints that answer and exits 0.
// STATUS: error
// CHECK: before
// COVERS: host-string exists
print "before";
print exists("/tmp/loxpp_probe_nul_exists" + chr(0) + "tail");
